  "notes": "{瞳|ひとみ} literally means the pupil of the eye, but is often used poetically to mean \"eyes\" in general.\n\nMEANINGS:\n1. {瞳孔|どうこう} (pupil) - the technical meaning\n2. Eyes - especially in literary or emotional contexts\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {瞳|ひとみ}が{輝|かがや}く: eyes sparkle\n- {澄|す}んだ{瞳|ひとみ}: clear eyes\n- {瞳|ひとみ}を{閉|と}じる: to close one's eyes (poetic)\n- {大|おお}きな{瞳|ひとみ}: big eyes\n\nREGISTER:\n{瞳|ひとみ} has a more literary, poetic, or romantic nuance compared to the everyday word {目|め}.\n\nNAME:\nCommon Japanese female name ({瞳|ひとみ}).\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {目|め}: eye (everyday word)\n- {眼|まなこ}: eye (literary/classical)\n- {瞳孔|どうこう}: pupil (medical term)",
